########## GATE 7j — size-band management concurrency (two real sessions) ##########
== case 1: two saves with the same expected version ==
  OK: exactly one same-version save won, the other got stale_layout after blocking; pollers saw only 5-band or 6-band complete layouts
== case 2a: save (held) vs assembly_add_line ==
  OK: the line waited for the layout commit and resolved xxl at layout version 2
== case 2b: assembly_add_line (held) vs save ==
  OK: the save waited for the in-flight line; the line kept the old layout snapshot (extra_large @ v1), the layout is v2
== case 3a: save (held) vs size-restricted package sale ==
  OK: the sale waited for the layout commit and was refused against the new layout
== case 3b: package sale (held) vs save ==
  OK: the save waited for the in-flight sale, saw the new entitlement, and was refused without any write
CONC PASS: same-version saves, save/line and save/sale (both orders) are serialized; no deadlock; no torn layout

